**Total first build target: $350–550.** All parts commodity and replaceable.

**BUILD·&·OPERATION·WORKFLOW**  
1. Assemble electronics on breadboard or protoboard first — test sensor reads.  
2. Build enclosure with compartments. Mount solar on top or side.  
3. Start first EM batch and first trap-culture pots same day.  
4. Daily/weekly: probe 3–5 spots in garden, read display, follow recommendation, apply.  
5. Log simple notes (notebook or optional local web page on Zero).  
6. Maintain cultures ongoing. Harvest mycorrhizae after one season.  
7. Iterate: add more sensors, bigger culture station, community data share if desired.

**SAFETY·&·LIMITATIONS·(HONEST)**  
Wear gloves when handling cultures. pH test fermentation. Start on small test bed. Cheap NPK sensors are trend tools, not lab accurate — cross-check with extension service yearly. Results depend on your local soil, climate, and consistency. This supports biology; it does not replace good organic practices (mulch, compost, minimal tillage). No GMOs, no synthetics.

